  "value": [
   {
    "statement": "The whole specification is inferred by claude-opus-5-5 subagent, 2026-10-29; it is not the official statement.",
    "basis": "preview fields used: contentPreview: a payment model for delivery dashers; pay depends on time spent on each order and on the number of concurrent deliveries; input is one dasher's order activities within one day; the pay rules themselves are cut off; algorithmTags: STRING, ARRAY; companies: DOORDASH; stage SCREENING; The inferring model recalls a commonly reported public version of this DoorDash screen: a per-minute base rate (about 0.3 dollars) multiplied by the number of ongoing orders, with follow-ups adding peak-hour multipliers; not verified against any source; preview response sha256 da33857c58a1849b3aa4cd69d283bbc3436c3af15884f2a65043770e3d621aef"
   },
   {
    "statement": "Uncertainty: very high: the preview names only the two pay factors (time per order, concurrent deliveries); the 30-cent base rate, linear concurrency multiplier, row format, event names, minute granularity, integer-cent output are invented; the split of rules across the three variants is invented",
    "basis": "the public group preview is partial (271 characters, group-level)"
   },
   {
    "statement": "Variant split: three variants share one preview with no per-variant text; inferred as cumulative follow-ups: variant 1 base rate times concurrency, variant 2 adds peak-hour doubling, variant 3 adds unpaid cancellations (invented)",
